        "Compute the majorities: a company has 1,000 ordinary shares, one vote each; 800 are present and voting, so a special resolution needs 600 yes votes, while an ordinary resolution needs 401. Small numbers make the arithmetic visible; large boards follow the same ratios. This counting exercise is the base drill of {S} meetings questions.",
